# Checked density of the binary 44-dimensional matrix pair

A polynomial in A+B+AB+BA gives a rank-one matrix. Its left and right
generator orbits have checked spanning bases. The binary matrix certificate
framework turns these checked XOR identities into equality with the full
matrix algebra. No group generation or irreducibility assumption is used.

The saved native witnesses and the untrusted emitter are in `source/`.
The native-action comparison is a separate obligation.
Source context: James (1973), pp.57--111; GM02 Proposition 5.1, p.17.
-/

